<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Optional, off by default: the cerebrex art setting draws Odyssey's cerebrex node
    (Apparel_CerebrexNode) with this mod's art in place of Odyssey's, one branch below per
    choice but Odyssey's own, which touches nothing and lets Odyssey's XML stand. The choices
    differ in what a dye paints (the node is colorable, ApparelNoQualityBase's CompColorable):

      DyeAll            our art, no mask: a dye tints the whole piece, as it does Odyssey's
      DyeFrame          our art and the masks that are red on the frame alone: the ring and
                        the core keep their own colors
      DyeFrameAndRing   our art and the masks that are red on the frame and the ring: only the
                        core keeps its red

    The node's art is two paths on the def: graphicData/texPath, the item on the ground and the
    icon the def resolves from it, and apparel/wornGraphicPath, the pack on the wearer's back
    (renderUtilityAsPack, so the worn path takes the facing suffixes and no body type one). Both
    take one path of ours, which Mods/Odyssey/Textures carries as the item (no suffix) and the
    three worn facings, never at Odyssey's path, where it would replace the art for everyone.

    A masked branch also turns the two mask switches on: graphicData/shaderType CutoutComplex
    for the item and apparel/useWornGraphicMask for the pack (ApparelGraphicRecordGetter picks
    the worn shader from that flag, never from graphicData). Odyssey's def sets neither field,
    so both are added. An undyed node draws white through either mask and looks as it does
    without one. The masks are found by name beside the art (_m for the item, _northm, _eastm
    and _southm for the pack, as the helmet's are named): the item's could sit elsewhere
    (graphicData/maskPath), but the worn graphic is built with no mask path
    (ApparelGraphicRecordGetter.TryGetGraphicApparel, 1.6 and 1.7.5000 decompiles), so each mask
    set needs a path of its own. DyeFrame's is CerebrexNodeOverlord, which DyeAll shares, its
    masks unread under a plain shader; DyeFrameAndRing's is CerebrexNodeOverlordRing, the same
    art copied beside the other masks.

    PatchOperationSetting reads the choice while the patches apply, so a change waits for a
    restart and the def then builds its graphic, icon and atlas entry from our path exactly as
    it would from Odyssey's. The root is gated on Odyssey's package id (LoadFolders.xml), so the
    xpaths never miss. The choices are CerebrexArt's names and the paths CerebrexNode.TexPath
    and RingTexPath (Source/1.6/Settings/CerebrexNode.cs), which the settings window reads off
    the def to show which art is live; Tests/1.6/CerebrexNodeArtTests.cs holds the branches,
    those names and constants and the shipped textures together.
  -->
  <Operation Class="OverlordWarcasket.PatchOperationSetting">
    <setting>cerebrexArt</setting>
    <choice>DyeAll</choice>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel/wornGraphicPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</wornGraphicPath>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="OverlordWarcasket.PatchOperationSetting">
    <setting>cerebrexArt</setting>
    <choice>DyeFrame</choice>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel/wornGraphicPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</wornGraphicPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel</xpath>
          <value>
            <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="OverlordWarcasket.PatchOperationSetting">
    <setting>cerebrexArt</setting>
    <choice>DyeFrameAndRing</choice>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlordRing/CerebrexNodePack</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel/wornGraphicPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlordRing/CerebrexNodePack</wornGraphicPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel</xpath>
          <value>
            <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
